  id: journal.ship_helmet
  title: "Read Your Visor"
  author: "Suit Tech M. Varga"
  dateLine: "Ship log 2187.03.05"
  category: 5
  body: "Your helmet visor comes up by itself whenever you step outside onto ground with no breathable air, and it drops again aboard the ship. It shows oxygen, nitrogen, CO2, the outside environment and suit integrity. Press H to raise or lower it if it gets in the way of fine work.\n\nIt's a readout, not a nanny. Glance at it every time you step out of the shuttle."
